From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivaylo Spasov <Ivaylo.Spasov@amd.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:19:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] radv/android: support deferred swapchain image binding

With VK_ANDROID_native_buffer v8+, the gralloc buffer backing an aliased
swapchain image is unknown at vkCreateImage() and only arrives in
VkNativeBufferANDROID at vkBindImageMemory2().

Follow PanVK, Venus, Turnip, and v3dv by using
vk_android_init_deferred_image() to preserve the create info. At bind
time, derive the explicit DRM modifier layout from the ANB, initialize
the RADV layout, import its memory, and continue through the normal bind
path.

Use the common vk_image.anb_memory ownership for both create-time and
deferred ANB imports, removing RADV's redundant owned_memory field.
Create-time imports use vkCreateImage()'s allocator; bind-time imports
use the device allocator because vkBindImageMemory2() has no allocation
callbacks.

Share deferred layout initialization with AHB and use vk_image_destroy()
to release common Android image state.

Fixes dEQP-VK.wsi.android.swapchain.create.image_swapchain_create_info
Fixes dEQP-VK.wsi.android.swapchain.simulate_oom.image_swapchain_create_info

Signed-off-by: Ivaylo Spasov <Ivaylo.Spasov@amd.com>
Assisted-by: Cursor
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44426>
(cherry picked from commit f7a9510280096eb223cfa954bb87d34ee41e9953)
